    "summary": "Addressed the three findings. (1) synthesize now calls assertMayAuthor a second time after finalizeArtifact returns and immediately before any path is computed or file written; plan-e2e.test.ts has a new test that walks a real plan to synthesize with a gate whose holder is the actor on the first ask and bob on every later ask, and shows synthesize returns team-gate-refused, asked the gate at least twice, and wrote no PLAN artifact. (2) runStart now calls assertMayAuthor(intent) as its first step inside its try block, so a refused run is an error frame from the entry, in addition to the driver's own entry and pre-write checks. (3) On 'before any state changes': decodeState must load the run state to learn the intent (the stage unit lives in the state), and that load refreshes the state's touchedAt expiry timestamp; that is the only effect, and it happens by necessity before the gate can know the unit. The refused phases write no artifact, run no executor, call no provider and save no new run state (the test asserts all of this, including the state-store size). The expiry refresh is bookkeeping of the controller's own continuation token, not a change to the stage.",
